.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
.TH V8MALLOC 3 "2026" "v8malloc 0.1.0" "v8malloc Library Functions"
.SH NAME
v8malloc \- high-performance memory allocator for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <v8malloc/v8malloc.h>
.PP
.BI "const char *v8m_version(void);"
.BI "int v8m_version_major(void);"
.BI "int v8m_version_minor(void);"
.BI "int v8m_version_patch(void);"
.fi
.PP
Link with
.BR \-lv8malloc " or preload " libv8malloc.so .
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B v8malloc
library is a drop-in replacement for the C runtime's
.BR malloc (3)
family, implementing a lock-free thread-local fast path, a
NUMA-aware tiered heap, explicit HugePage management, and a header-less
per-page metadata layout.
.PP
Once loaded, v8malloc services every standard allocation call
.RB ( malloc (3),
.BR free (3),
.BR calloc (3),
.BR realloc (3),
.BR posix_memalign (3),
.BR aligned_alloc (3), ...)
with behavior conformant to POSIX.1-2024. This manual page documents
only the v8malloc-specific extensions; see the referenced manual pages
for the base semantics.
.SH VERSION FUNCTIONS
The functions listed in
.B SYNOPSIS
report the library's runtime version.
.B v8m_version()
returns a pointer to a static string of the form
.RI "\(dq" MAJOR . MINOR . PATCH \(dq ,
identical to the
.B V8M_VERSION_STRING
macro the caller was compiled against. The numeric accessors return the
corresponding integer components.
.SH USAGE
.SS LD_PRELOAD
.PP
.nf
LD_PRELOAD=/usr/lib/libv8malloc.so ./your-program
.fi
.SS Direct linking
.PP
.nf
cc -o myapp myapp.c -lv8malloc -lpthread -ldl
.fi
.SS CMake
.PP
.nf
find_package(v8malloc REQUIRED)
target_link_libraries(myapp PRIVATE v8malloc::v8malloc)
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
v8malloc reads the following variables at library initialization:
.TP
.B V8M_VERBOSE
When set to
.B 1 ,
emit allocator statistics to stderr at shutdown.
.TP
.B V8M_PURGE_INTERVAL
Background memory-return interval, in seconds. Default: 10.
.TP
.B V8M_THREAD_CACHE_MAX
Maximum number of objects held per size-class in the thread cache.
.TP
.B V8M_HUGE_PAGES
When
.B 0 ,
disables explicit HugePage allocation.
.TP
.B V8M_NUMA_AWARE
When
.B 0 ,
disables NUMA-aware placement and binding.
.TP
.B V8M_DEBUG
When
.B 1 ,
enables guard pages, red-zone checking, double-free detection, and
leak reporting. Incurs significant runtime cost.
.TP
.B V8M_PROFILE
When
.B 1 ,
enables profiling-mode output.
.SH BUGS
Report defects via the GitHub issue tracker referenced in
.BR README.md ;
security-sensitive issues should follow
.BR SECURITY.md .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR malloc (3),
.BR posix_memalign (3),
.BR mallopt (3),
.BR mmap (2),
.BR madvise (2),
.BR mbind (2),
.BR ld.so (8)
